# CCNP/CCIE Automation — AUTOCOR 350-901 v2.0 Blueprint Alignment

The learner is preparing for both cloud SE interviews AND the Cisco CCNP Automation certification (core exam: 350-901 AUTOCOR v2.0). When helping with any module, exercise, or project, actively reinforce exam topics whenever the opportunity arises naturally.

NOTE: The old DEVCOR v1.1 exam has been retired. The current exam is AUTOCOR v2.0 — "Designing, Deploying and Managing Network Automation Systems." Do NOT reference DEVCOR topics that were dropped (Webex Teams, Firepower FDM, UCS, Intersight, AppDynamics, NSO, Kubernetes, OAuth2 three-legged flow, 12-factor app, database types, architectural patterns).

## AUTOCOR v2.0 Blueprint (4 Domains)

### 1.0 Network Automation (30%)
- 1.1 Construct automation with **Ansible** (VLANs, OSPF, asset mgmt, interfaces, ACLs)
- 1.2 Construct automation with **Terraform** (VLANs, OSPF, asset mgmt, interfaces, ACLs)
- 1.3 Construct automation with **RESTCONF** (RFC 8040) given a YANG model (VLANs, OSPF, interfaces, ACLs)
- 1.4 Construct automation with **Python** (VLANs, OSPF, asset mgmt, interfaces, ACLs)
- 1.5 **Select** the right automation approach (IaC framework vs low-code/no-code vs custom app)
- 1.6 Consume **REST APIs** with pagination, complex auth workflows, rate limiting, error handling, persistent auth

### 2.0 Infrastructure as Code (30%)
- 2.1 Advanced **Git** operations:
  - 2.1.a Merge (including squash and conflict resolution)
  - 2.1.b git cherry-pick
  - 2.1.c git reset
  - 2.1.d git checkout
  - 2.1.e git revert
- 2.2 Additional IaC topics: **CML automation** (REST API, PyCML), **Docker Compose**, **source of truth** (NetBox/Nautobot), YANG-to-YAML/JSON payload generation
- 2.3 Construct a **GitLab CE CI/CD pipeline** with stages:
  - 2.3.a build
  - 2.3.b prevalidation
  - 2.3.c deploy
  - 2.3.d post-validation

### 3.0 Operations (20%)
- 3.1 Describe architectural components of **model-driven telemetry** (gRPC dial-in/dial-out, data types, cadence)
- 3.2 Implement a **logging strategy** (syslog, webhooks)
- 3.3 **Diagnose** problems given logs and output
- 3.4 Implement **change validation** with **pyATS** CLI tools
- 3.5 Describe obtaining and deploying **CA-signed TLS certificates**
- 3.6 Implement **secure coding**: input validation, authentication, secret management

### 4.0 AI in Automation (20%)
- 4.1 Describe benefits and risks of **AI-assisted code development** (data privacy, IP ownership, code validation)
- 4.2 Interpret **security risks** in AI-based automation (prompt injection, RAG poisoning, over-permissive tools)
- 4.3 Construct an **MCP server** with **Python FastMCP** to provide network info to an AI agent
- 4.4 Construct a **conversational agent** using **LLMs** for network automation
- 4.5 Evaluate **accuracy** of AI recommendations on automation solutions

## How to Apply This Rule

- When teaching Python or Ansible or Terraform, frame exercises around the specific config tasks from Domain 1 (VLANs, OSPF, interfaces, ACLs)
- When working on REST APIs (Module 3, 4), demonstrate pagination, error handling, rate limiting, and persistent auth per Domain 1.6
- When covering Git (GitHub Workflow), teach advanced operations from Domain 2.1 (squash merge, cherry-pick, reset, revert)
- When covering CI/CD (Module 9), note the exam specifies GitLab CE, not GitHub Actions — mention the difference and suggest the learner set up a free GitLab CE instance alongside GitHub
- When covering testing (Module 7), emphasize pyATS CLI tools specifically per Domain 3.4
- When covering NETCONF/YANG (Module 5), connect to model-driven telemetry per Domain 3.1
- When covering Azure AI (Module 4.5), connect to Domain 4 (AI in Automation) — expand to cover MCP servers, FastMCP, LLM agents, and AI risk assessment
- Do NOT turn every session into exam prep — the primary goal is building projects. Weave blueprint topics in naturally.
- When a gap topic comes up, mention the AUTOCOR domain and suggest where to learn more.
- The learner is a beginner but wants to go all the way to advanced level in all three domain of network automation, cloud networking and computer enterprisecnetworking learning in genera. To a good level where they can creack interviews. Explain them all the concepts with hands-on approach so the learning really sticks.The topics and explanation should be comprehensive. 

